    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem description\n\nAfter following your fantastic documentation on the inner works of `vim.pack.add`, I have attempted to replicate the `build` flag that some package managers like LazyVim offer to pre-build the packages before loading them. Following your example on the `TSUpdate` hook, I have attempted the following for `telescope.nvim`:\n\n```lua\nnow_if_args(function()\n  -- Define hook to build telescope and its dependencies\n  local build = function(plugin_name)\n    local path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/core/opt/' .. plugin_name\n    local res = vim.system({ 'make', '-C', path }, { text = true }):wait()\n    if res.code ~= 0 then\n      vim.notify('Build failed: ' .. res.stderr, vim.log.levels.ERROR); return\n    end\n  end\n  Config.on_packchanged('telescope.nvim', { 'install', 'update' }, function() build('telescope.nvim') end,\n    'Build telescope')\n  Config.on_packchanged('telescope-fzf-native.nvim', { 'install', 'update' },\n    function() build('telescope-fzf-native.nvim') end,\n    'Build telescope-fzf-native')\n  vim.pack.add({ \"https://github.com/nvim-telescope/telescope-fzf-native.nvim\" },\n    { \"https://github.com/nvim-telescope/telescope.nvim\" }\n  )\nend)\n```\n\nHowever, this does not seem to work, since `:Telescope` is not available after restarting neovim.  Would you be able to add an example for such a pre-build process in a plugin? I think this would cover most of the hooks for package management that we can find in `LazyVim`, namely, `cmd`, `event` and `build`. WDYT?",
