        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thank you so much for your reply  😄  The table argument was indeed the problem. I missed it since it was silently failing, as you mention. The `callback` argument is a nice extra trick. I got the config working now.\n\n> The cmd and event are not really for package management, but for lazy loading.\n\nOk, but they are \"features\" most pkg managers offer and plugins explicitly show in their installation sections. So having a way to translate them into standard lua configuration will make it easier for users to migrate to `vim.pack.add`.\n\n",
